# Personal agent defaults

Apply these after any repository `AGENTS.md`. The full text is `~/.agents/AGENTS.md`.

- Separate how a behavior is called from how it is implemented.
- Add a test only when an observable responsibility boundary changes.
- Do not create or draft PR/MR titles or bodies. Return bullet material only when asked.
- Put the conclusion first. Keep facts, conditions, and uncertainty.

Shared skills live in `~/.agents/skills/`:

- `responsibility-boundary` for implementation and bug fixes
- `claim-review` for review-only claim and boundary checks
- `handoff` for explicit save or resume

This file is deployed to `~/.cursor/rules/`. Cursor loads `.cursor/rules` by walking ancestors of the workspace. A checkout whose path does not pass through `$HOME` does not load it. Put the same file in that project's `.cursor/rules/` when the checkout is outside `$HOME`.
